Relevant columns (and why)

• fullVisitorId: unique visitor key – use to stitch all sessions belonging to the same user.  
• visitStartTime: session Unix‑epoch – use to derive first‑visit date and all “event” dates.  
• date: YYYYMMDD string version of the visit date – handy to turn epoch into a calendar day.  
• totals.transactions: number of transactions in the session – if >0 → the session contains the first transaction.  
• device.isMobile: TRUE/FALSE flag telling whether the session happened on a mobile device – we keep only users whose last recorded event is mobile.  
• _TABLE_SUFFIX (virtual) : the wild‑card part after ga_sessions_* – lets us query many day‑tables at once and/or filter a time range.  

Typical conditions

• totals.transactions > 0 → “transaction sessions”.  
• device.isMobile = TRUE → sessions that occurred on a mobile device.  
• _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20160801' AND '20170801' → limit to the 1‑year demo data range.  


Ten exploratory → final SQL snippets
(each limited to 20 rows and wrapped in back‑ticks for copy/paste)

```sql
-- 1. Peek at raw rows (20 random sessions)
